    RowBox[{"x", ",", 
     RowBox[{"{", "\"\<something new\>\"", "}"}], ",", "z"}], 
    "}"}]}]}]], "Input"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
  Example: Find Your Telephone Extension In \[Pi]:\
\>", "Subsection"],

Cell["\<\
My TU telephone extension is:  2983.  Exactly where are these digits located \
in the number \[Pi]?\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.3898373265066557`*^9, 3.3898373284046555`*^9}}],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"pi", "=", 
  RowBox[{"N", "[", 
   RowBox[{"\[Pi]", ",", "40"}], "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.389837287516656*^9, 3.3898372882086554`*^9}}],

Cell["\<\

In order to use pattern matching, we need a list (of characters).  The \
precise characters depend upon the format that the number is represented in.  \
Thus, our first command is to have a number converted to a string \
corresponding to the desired output format.  Then, convert the string to a \
list of characters.  Once we have a list, then we can use pattern matching to \
locate my TU telephone extension.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.523276988494827*^9}],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
ToString[expr] gives a string corresponding to the printed form of expr in \
OutputForm.
ToString[expr, form] gives the string corresponding to output in the \
specified form.\
\>", "Item",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.3900435453134003`*^9, 3.3900435550334*^9}},
 FontWeight->"Bold"],

Cell["\<\
Characters \"string\" gives a list of the characters in a string.\
\>", "Item",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.3900435492904*^9, 3.3900435532264*^9}},
 FontWeight->"Bold"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{" ", 
  RowBox[{"piList", " ", "=", 
   RowBox[{"Characters", " ", "[", 
    RowBox[{"ToString", "[", "pi", "]"}], "]"}]}]}]], "Input"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{" ", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"findNumber", " ", "[", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"a___", ",", "\"\<2\>\"", ",", "b___"}], "}"}], "]"}], ":=", 
   RowBox[{"{", "a", "}"}]}]}]], "InputOnly"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{" ", 
  RowBox[{"findNumber", " ", "[", "piList", "]"}]}]], "Input"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Clear", "[", "findNumber", "]"}]], "InputOnly"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{" ", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"findNumber", " ", "[", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
     "a___", ",", "\"\<2\>\"", ",", "\"\<9\>\"", ",", "\"\<8\>\"", ",", 
      "\"\<3\>\"", ",", "b___"}], "}"}], "]"}], ":=", "\n", "\t            ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
    "a", ",", "\"\<**2983**\>\"", ",", 
     "\"\< The number of decimal places is = \>\"", ",", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Length", "[", 
       RowBox[{"{", "a", "}"}], "]"}], "-", "2"}]}], "}"}]}]}]], "InputOnly"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"findNumber", " ", "[", "piList", "]"}]], "Input"],

Cell["\<\

Note that no pattern match was found for this list of 10 digits.  Thus, try \
1000.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.5232770335852776`*^9}],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"piList", " ", "=", 
   RowBox[{"Characters", " ", "[", 
    RowBox[{"ToString", "[", 
     RowBox[{"N", "[", 
      RowBox[{"\[Pi]", ",", "1000"}], "]"}], "]"}], "]"}]}], ";"}]], "Input"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"findNumber", " ", "[", "piList", "]"}]], "Input"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"N", "[", 
  RowBox[{"\[Pi]", ",", "504"}], "]"}]], "Input"]
}, Closed]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
  Example: Passing An Unspecified List Of Options (Functional Arguments):\
\>", "Subsection"],

Cell["\<\
One important use of pattern matching (of zero or more arguments) is passing \
an unspecified list of arguments to a function or a module.\
\>", "Text"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Clear", "[", "myPlot", "]"}]], "InputOnly"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"myPlot", "[", 
   RowBox[{"f_", ",", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"x_", ",", "xmin_", ",", "xmax_"}], "}"}], ",", "opts___"}], 
   "]"}], ":=", "\[IndentingNewLine]", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
  RowBox[{"Plot", "[", "\[IndentingNewLine]", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
   RowBox[{"f", ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"x", ",", "xmin", ",", "xmax"}], "}"}], ",", 
    "\[IndentingNewLine]", "\[IndentingNewLine]", "opts"}], 
   "\[IndentingNewLine]", "\[IndentingNewLine]", "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.3898374509896555`*^9, 3.389837470011656*^9}}],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"??", "myPlot"}]], "Input"],

Cell["\<\

Make a call with zero options.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.52327707179566*^9}],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"myPlot", "[", "\[IndentingNewLine]", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Sin", "[", "x", "]"}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
   "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"x", ",", "0", ",", 
     RowBox[{"2", "\[Pi]"}]}], "}"}]}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
  "\[IndentingNewLine]", "]"}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.3898374909896555`*^9, 3.3898375170026555`*^9}}],

Cell["\<\

Make a call with one option.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.523277075405696*^9}],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"myPlot", "[", "\[IndentingNewLine]", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Sin", "[", "x", "]"}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
   "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"x", ",", "0", ",", 
     RowBox[{"2", "\[Pi]"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
   "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
   RowBox[{"PlotLabel", "\[Rule]", "\"\<One Option!\>\""}]}], 
  "\[IndentingNewLine]", "\[IndentingNewLine]", "]"}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.389837501735656*^9, 3.3898375321306553`*^9}, {
  3.3898377255506554`*^9, 3.389837733610656*^9}}],

Cell["\<\

Make a call with two options.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.5232770785257273`*^9}],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"myPlot", "[", "\[IndentingNewLine]", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Sin", "[", "x", "]"}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
   "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"x", ",", "0", ",", 
     RowBox[{"2", " ", "\[Pi]"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
   "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
   RowBox[{"PlotStyle", "\[Rule]", 
    RowBox[{"Thickness", "[", ".02", "]"}]}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
   RowBox[{"PlotLabel", "\[Rule]", "\"\<Two Options!\>\""}]}], 
  "\[IndentingNewLine]", "\[IndentingNewLine]", "]"}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.3898375399606557`*^9, 3.3898376989426556`*^9}}]
}, Closed]]
}, Closed]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[TextData[StyleBox["  Pattern Matching And Delayed Assignments:", \
"Subtitle"]], "Section"],

Cell["\<\
As illustrated above, if assignments and replacements are not delayed, then \
it is possible that undesired assignments and replacements could be made.
\
\>", "Text"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
lhs = rhs evaluates rhs and assigns the result to be the value of lhs. From \
then on, lhs is replaced by rhs whenever it appears. \
\>", "Item",
 GeneratedCell->False,
 CellAutoOverwrite->False,
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.3900435173164*^9, 3.3900435266684*^9}},
 FontWeight->"Bold"],

Cell["\<\
lhs := rhs assigns rhs to be the delayed value of lhs. rhs is maintained in \
an unevaluated form. When lhs appears, it is replaced by rhs, evaluated \
afresh each time.\
\>", "Item",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.3900435194184*^9, 3.3900435286624002`*^9}},
 FontWeight->"Bold"],

Cell["lhs -> rhs represents a rule that transforms lhs to rhs.", "Item",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.3900435209614*^9, 3.3900435297944*^9}},
 FontWeight->"Bold"],

Cell["\<\
lhs :> rhs represents a rule that transforms lhs to rhs, evaluating rhs only \
when the rule is used.\
\>", "Item",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.3900435229494*^9, 3.3900435316814003`*^9}},
 FontWeight->"Bold"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[TextData[StyleBox[" Assignments And Delayed Assignments,\n Rules And \
Delayed Rules:",
 FontSize->16]], "Subsection"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[" Immediate Assignments:", "Subsubsection"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Every operation in ",
 StyleBox["Mathematica",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " has an equivalent functional form.  \nFor an assignment, i.e. \"",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"lhs", "=", "rhs"}], TraditionalForm]]],
 "\" the corresponding command is: ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"Set", "[", 
    RowBox[{"lhs", ",", "rhs"}], "]"}], TraditionalForm]]],
 ".  \nFor a delayed assignment, i.e. \"",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{":", " ", "="}], TraditionalForm]]],
 "\" the corresponding command is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"SetDelayed", "[", 
    RowBox[{"lhs", ",", "rhs"}], "]"}], TraditionalForm]]],
 "."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.3898377882986555`*^9, 3.389837856832656*^9}}],

Cell["\<\
lhs = rhs evaluates rhs and assigns the result to be the value of lhs. From \
then on, lhs is replaced by rhs whenever it appears.\
\>", "Item",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.3900435088914003`*^9, 3.3900435111504*^9}},
 FontWeight->"Bold"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"  ", 
  RowBox[{"Attributes", " ", "[", "Set", "]"}]}]], "Input"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "\nNote that Set has attribute ",
 StyleBox["HoldFirst",
  FontVariations->{"Underline"->True}],
 ".  This means that the assignment of the rhs to the lhs will be made before \
the lhs is evaluated.  Thus, even if the lhs has an assigned value, it will \
be replaced with the rhs before this assigned value is used."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.523277136946311*^9}],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Clear", " ", "[", 
  RowBox[{"a", ",", "b"}], "]"}]], "InputOnly",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.389837907247656*^9, 3.389837908676656*^9}}],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"a", "=", "2"}]], "Input"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"a", "=", "b"}]], "Input"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Print", "[", 
  RowBox[{"\"\<a = \>\"", ",", "a", ",", "\"\<     b = \>\"", ",", "b"}], 
  "]"}]], "Input"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "\nThe above assignment is evaluated as:\n\n\t",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"a", "=", "2"}], TraditionalForm]]],
 "\n\t",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"a", "=", "b"}], TraditionalForm]]],
 "         (Note that the assignment is made before \"a\" is evaluated)\n\t",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["b", TraditionalForm]]]
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.3898379411396556`*^9, 3.3898379503626556`*^9}, 
   3.523277155396496*^9}],

Cell["\<\
In what follows, note that the assignment to the rhs is made before assigning \
its value to the lhs.  Thus, even if we change the value of the rhs after the \
assignment, it will not take on the new value.\
\>", "Text"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Clear", " ", "[", 
  RowBox[{"a", ",", "b"}], "]"}]], "InputOnly",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.3898379667046556`*^9, 3.3898379669656553`*^9}}],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"a", "=", "2"}], ";", 
  RowBox[{"b", "=", "3"}], ";"}]], "InputOnly"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Print", "[", 
  RowBox[{"\"\<a = \>\"", ",", "a", ",", "\"\<     b = \>\"", ",", "b"}], 
  "]"}]], "Input"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"a", "=", "b"}]], "Input"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Print", "[", 
  RowBox[{"\"\<a = \>\"", ",", "a", ",", "\"\<     b = \>\"", ",", "b"}], 
  "]"}]], "Input"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"b", "=", "5"}]], "Input"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Print", "[", 
  RowBox[{"\"\<a = \>\"", ",", "a", ",", "\"\<     b = \>\"", ",", "b"}], 
  "]"}]], "Input"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "\nThe above assignment is evaluated as:\n\n\t",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"a", "=", "2"}], " ", ";", " ", 
    RowBox[{"b", "=", "3"}]}], TraditionalForm]]],
 "\n\t",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"a", "=", "b"}], TraditionalForm]]],
 "\n\t",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"a", "=", "3"}], TraditionalForm]]],
 " \t(Note that the value of \"b\" is evaluated first)\n\t3 \t(Note that the \
assignment is made before \"a\" is evaluated)\n  \t\t(Note the assignment: ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"b", "=", "5"}], TraditionalForm]]],
 ")"
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.3898379905346556`*^9, 3.389838017070656*^9}, 
   3.5232772252871947`*^9}]
}, Closed]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[" Delayed Assignments:", "Subsubsection"],

Cell["\<\
lhs := rhs assigns rhs to be the delayed value of lhs. rhs is maintained in \
an unevaluated form. When lhs appears, it is replaced by rhs, evaluated \
afresh each time.\
\>", "Item",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.3900435010634003`*^9, 3.3900435042344*^9}},
 FontWeight->"Bold"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"  ", 
  RowBox[{"Attributes", " ", "[", "SetDelayed", "]"}]}]], "Input"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "\nNote that ",
 StyleBox["HoldAll",
  FontVariations->{"Underline"->True}],
 " is an attribute of SetDelayed.  Thus, a new value for the rhs can be \
assigned after the delayed assignment has been made and the lhs will be \
assigned this new value."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.523277261127553*^9}],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Clear", " ", "[", 
  RowBox[{"a", ",", "b"}], "]"}]], "InputOnly",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.3898380487816553`*^9, 3.3898380489806557`*^9}}],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"a", "=", "2"}], ";", 
  RowBox[{"b", "=", "3"}], ";"}]], "InputOnly"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Print", "[", 
  RowBox[{"\"\<a = \>\"", ",", "a", ",", "\"\<     b = \>\"", ",", "b"}], 
  "]"}]], "Input"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"a", ":=", "b"}]], "InputOnly"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Print", "[", 
  RowBox[{"\"\<a = \>\"", ",", "a", ",", "\"\<     b = \>\"", ",", "b"}], 
  "]"}]], "Input"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"b", "=", "5"}]], "Input"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Print", "[", 
  RowBox[{"\"\<a = \>\"", ",", "a", ",", "\"\<     b = \>\"", ",", "b"}], 
  "]"}]], "Input"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "\nThe above assignment is evaluated as:\n\n\t",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"a", "=", "2"}], " ", ";", " ", 
    RowBox[{"b", "=", "3"}]}], TraditionalForm]]],
 "\n\t",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"a", ":=", "b"}], TraditionalForm]]],
 "\n\t",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"b", "=", "5"}], TraditionalForm]]],
 "\n\tEvaluate: ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["a", TraditionalForm]]],
 ",  where:  ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"a", ":=", "b"}], TraditionalForm]]],
 "\n\t",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"a", ":=", "5"}], TraditionalForm]]],
 "\t(Note that the value of \"b\" is evaluated first)\n\t5\t(Note that the \
assignment is made before \"a\" is evaluated)\n  \t\t(Note the assignment: ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"b", "=", "5"}], TraditionalForm]]],
 ")"
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.3898381838006554`*^9, 3.3898382379286556`*^9}, 
   3.5232772793977356`*^9}]
}, Closed]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[" Immediate Replacement Rules, Example 1:", "Subsubsection"],

Cell["\<\
The functional form for a rule   \"lhs \[Rule] rhs\"   is:  Rule[lhs, rhs].\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.389838249478656*^9, 3.3898382555766554`*^9}}],

Cell["lhs -> rhs represents a rule that transforms lhs to rhs.", "Item",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.3900434937644*^9, 3.3900434968864*^9}},
 FontWeight->"Bold"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"  ", 
  RowBox[{"Attributes", " ", "[", "Rule", "]"}]}]], "Input"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "\nNote that ",
 StyleBox["neither",
  FontVariations->{"Underline"->True}],
 " the lhs or rhs is held from evaluation before the rule is used.  Thus, ",
 StyleBox["any",
  FontVariations->{"Underline"->True}],
 " assignments to the lhs or the rhs will be evaluated ",
 StyleBox["before",
  FontVariations->{"Underline"->True}],
 " the rule is invoked."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.5232773118480606`*^9}],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Clear", " ", "[", 
  RowBox[{"a", ",", "b", ",", "c"}], "]"}]], "InputOnly",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.3898383060906553`*^9, 3.3898383065416555`*^9}}],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"a", "=", "2"}], ";", 
  RowBox[{"b", "=", "3"}], ";", 
  RowBox[{"c", "=", "4"}], ";"}]], "InputOnly"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Print", "[", 
  RowBox[{
  "\"\<a = \>\"", ",", "a", ",", "\"\<     b = \>\"", ",", "b", ",", 
   "\"\<     c = \>\"", ",", "c"}], "]"}]], "Input"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{" ", 
  RowBox[{"rule1", "=", 
   RowBox[{"b", "\[Rule]", "c"}]}]}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.389838339334656*^9, 3.389838343176656*^9}}],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Print", "[", 
  RowBox[{
  "\"\<a = \>\"", ",", "a", ",", "\"\<     b = \>\"", ",", "b", ",", 
   "\"\<     c = \>\"", ",", "c", ",", "\"\<     rule1 = \>\"", ",", 
   "rule1"}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.3898384469546556`*^9, 3.3898384808826556`*^9}}],

Cell["\<\

Note that BOTH the lhs and the rhs in rule1 have been changed from a and b.
Change the value of \"b\": \
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.3898383603096557`*^9, 3.3898383831496553`*^9}, {
   3.3898385624416556`*^9, 3.389838610860656*^9}, 3.523277340288345*^9}],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"b", "=", "5"}]], "Input"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Print", "[", 
  RowBox[{
  "\"\<a = \>\"", ",", "a", ",", "\"\<     b = \>\"", ",", "b", ",", 
   "\"\<     c = \>\"", ",", "c", ",", "\"\<     rule1 = \>\"", ",", 
   "rule1"}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.3898384469546556`*^9, 3.3898384808826556`*^9}}],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"a", ":=", 
  RowBox[{"b", " ", "/.", "rule1"}]}]], "InputOnly"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"?", "a"}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.3898386694516554`*^9, 3.3898387134096556`*^9}],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Print", "[", 
  RowBox[{
  "\"\<a = \>\"", ",", "a", ",", "\"\<     b = \>\"", ",", "b", ",", 
   "\"\<     c = \>\"", ",", "c", ",", "\"\<     rule1 = \>\"", ",", 
   "rule1"}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.3898384469546556`*^9, 3.3898384808826556`*^9}}],

Cell[TextData[{
 "\n Thus, the above replacement rule is evaluated as:\n\n\t",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"a", "=", "2"}], ";", 
    RowBox[{"b", "=", "3"}], ";", 
    RowBox[{"c", "=", "4"}], ";"}], TraditionalForm]]],
 "\n\t",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"rule1", "=", 
    RowBox[{"b", "\[Rule]", "c"}]}], TraditionalForm]]],
 "\n\t",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"rule1", "=", 
    RowBox[{"3", "\[Rule]", "4"}]}], TraditionalForm]]],
 "  \t(Note immediate replacement of both the lhs and rhs)\n\t",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"b", "=", "5"}], ";"}], TraditionalForm]]],
 "\n\t",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"a", ":=", 
    RowBox[{"b", "  ", "/.", "  ", "rule1"}]}], TraditionalForm]]],
 "\n\t",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"a", ":=", 
    RowBox[{"5", "  ", "/.", "  ", "rule1"}]}], TraditionalForm]]],
 "  \t(\"b\" is replaced by 5)\n\t",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"a", ":=", 
    RowBox[{"5", "  ", "/.", "  ", 
     RowBox[{"3", "\[Rule]", "4"}]}]}], TraditionalForm]]],
 "\n\t",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"a", ":=", 
    RowBox[{"5", "  ", "/.", "  ", 
     RowBox[{"3", "\[Rule]", "4"}]}]}], TraditionalForm]]],
 "\t(Note that the rule is not used)\n\t",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"a", ":=", "5"}], TraditionalForm]]],
 "\n\t5   \t\t\t(",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"b", "=", "5"}], ",", 
    RowBox[{"c", "=", "4"}]}], TraditionalForm]]],
 ")"
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.389838422169656*^9, 3.3898384338266554`*^9}, {
   3.3898387564966555`*^9, 3.389838823983656*^9}, {3.3898390269636555`*^9, 
   3.3898390618676558`*^9}, 3.5232773895088367`*^9}]
}, Closed]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[" Immediate Replacement Rules, Example 2:", "Subsubsection"],

Cell["\<\
A small variation of the above procedure keeps the value of \"b\" the same:\
\>", "Text"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"  ", 
  RowBox[{"Clear", " ", "[", 
   RowBox[{"a", ",", "b", ",", "c"}], "]"}]}]], "InputOnly"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"a", "=", "2"}], ";", 
  RowBox[{"b", "=", "3"}], ";", 
  RowBox[{"c", "=", "4"}], ";"}]], "InputOnly"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{" ", 
  RowBox[{"rule1", "=", 
   RowBox[{"b", "\[Rule]", "c"}]}]}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.389838839108656*^9, 3.3898388403686557`*^9}}],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Print", "[", 
  RowBox[{
  "\"\<a = \>\"", ",", "a", ",", "\"\<     b = \>\"", ",", "b", ",", 
   "\"\<     c = \>\"", ",", "c", ",", "\"\<     rule1 = \>\"", ",", 
   "rule1"}], "]"}]], "Input"],

Cell["\<\

Keep the value of \"b\" the same:\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.523277435199294*^9}],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"b", "=", "3"}]], "Input"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"a", ":=", 
  RowBox[{"b", " ", "/.", "rule1"}]}]], "InputOnly"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"?", "a"}]], "Input"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Print", "[", 
  RowBox[{
  "\"\<a = \>\"", ",", "a", ",", "\"\<     b = \>\"", ",", "b", ",", 
   "\"\<     c = \>\"", ",", "c", ",", "\"\<     rule1 = \>\"", ",", 
   "rule1"}], "]"}]], "Input"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "\nThus, the above replacement rule is evaluated as:\n\n\t",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"a", "=", "2"}], ";", 
    RowBox[{"b", "=", "3"}], ";", 
    RowBox[{"c", "=", "4"}], ";"}], TraditionalForm]]],
 "\n\t",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"rule1", "=", 
    RowBox[{"b", "\[Rule]", "c"}]}], TraditionalForm]]],
 "\n\t",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"rule1", "=", 
    RowBox[{"3", "\[Rule]", "4"}]}], TraditionalForm]]],
 "\t\t(Note immediate replacement of both the lhs and rhs)\n\t",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"a", ":=", 
    RowBox[{"b", "  ", "/.", "  ", "rule1"}]}], TraditionalForm]]],
 "\n\t",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"a", ":=", 
    RowBox[{"3", "  ", "/.", "  ", "rule1"}]}], TraditionalForm]]],
 "\t(\"b\" is replaced by 3)\n\t",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"a", ":=", 
    RowBox[{"3", "  ", "/.", "  ", 
     RowBox[{"3", "\[Rule]", "4"}]}]}], TraditionalForm]]],
 "\n\t",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"a", ":=", 
    RowBox[{"3", "  ", "/.", "  ", 
     RowBox[{"3", "\[Rule]", "4"}]}]}], TraditionalForm]]],
 "\t(Note that \"b\" has the value 3 because it was not changed)\n\t",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"a", ":=", "4"}], TraditionalForm]]],
 "\t\t\t(Thus, the replacement is used\n\t    \t\t\teven though \"b\" has \
been assigned to be 3)\n\t4\t\t\t(",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"b", "=", "3"}], ",", 
    RowBox[{"c", "=", "4"}]}], TraditionalForm]]],
 ")"
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.3898388510416555`*^9, 3.3898388628686557`*^9}, {
   3.389838961839656*^9, 3.3898390098776555`*^9}, {3.3898390810466557`*^9, 
   3.3898391170476556`*^9}, 3.5232774421393633`*^9}]
}, Closed]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[" Immediate Replacement Rules, Example 3:", "Subsubsection"],

Cell["\<\
Another small variation is to use immediate assignment along with the \
immediate rule:\
\>", "Text"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"  ", 
  RowBox[{"Clear", " ", "[", 
   RowBox[{"a", ",", "b", ",", "c"}], "]"}]}]], "InputOnly"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"a", "=", "2"}], ";", 
  RowBox[{"b", "=", "3"}], ";", 
  RowBox[{"c", "=", "4"}], ";"}]], "InputOnly"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{" ", 
  RowBox[{"rule1", "=", 
   RowBox[{"b", "\[Rule]", "c"}]}]}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.389839160379656*^9, 3.389839161202656*^9}}],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Print", "[", 
  RowBox[{
  "\"\<a = \>\"", ",", "a", ",", "\"\<     b = \>\"", ",", "b", ",", 
   "\"\<     c = \>\"", ",", "c", ",", "\"\<     rule1 = \>\"", ",", 
   "rule1"}], "]"}]], "Input"],

Cell["\<\

Change the value of \"b\":\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.5232775198401403`*^9}],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"b", "=", "5"}]], "Input"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"a", "=", 
  RowBox[{"b", " ", "/.", "rule1"}]}]], "Input"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"?", "a"}]], "Input"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Print", "[", 
  RowBox[{
  "\"\<a = \>\"", ",", "a", ",", "\"\<     b = \>\"", ",", "b", ",", 
   "\"\<     c = \>\"", ",", "c", ",", "\"\<     rule1 = \>\"", ",", 
   "rule1"}], "]"}]], "Input"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "\nThus, the above replacement rule with immediate assignment is evaluated \
as:\n\n\t",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"a", "=", "2"}], ";", 
    RowBox[{"b", "=", "3"}], ";", 
    RowBox[{"c", "=", "4"}], ";"}], TraditionalForm]]],
 "\n\t",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"rule1", "=", 
    RowBox[{"b", "\[Rule]", "c"}]}], TraditionalForm]]],
 "\n\t",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"rule1", "=", 
    RowBox[{"3", "\[Rule]", "4"}]}], TraditionalForm]]],
 "\t\t(Note immediate replacement of both the lhs and rhs)\n\t",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"b", "=", "5"}], ";"}], TraditionalForm]]],
 "\n\t",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"a", "=", 
    RowBox[{"b", "  ", "/.", "  ", "rule1"}]}], TraditionalForm]]],
 "\n\t",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"a", "=", 
    RowBox[{"5", "  ", "/.", "  ", "rule1"}]}], TraditionalForm]]],
 "\t(\"b\" is replaced by 5)\n\t",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"a", "=", 
    RowBox[{"5", "  ", "/.", "  ", 
     RowBox[{"3", "\[Rule]", "4"}]}]}], TraditionalForm]]],
 "\n\t",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"a", "=", 
    RowBox[{"5", "  ", "/.", "  ", 
     RowBox[{"3", "\[Rule]", "4"}]}]}], TraditionalForm]]],
 "\t(Note that the rule is not used)\n\t",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"a", "=", "5"}], TraditionalForm]]],
 "\n\t5 \t\t\t(",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"b", "=", "5"}], ",", 
    RowBox[{"c", "=", "4"}]}], TraditionalForm]]],
 ")\n"
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.3898391860146556`*^9, 3.389839227134656*^9}, {
   3.3898393056786556`*^9, 3.389839357419656*^9}, {3.3898396326616554`*^9, 
   3.3898396389846554`*^9}, 3.523277526010202*^9}]
}, Closed]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[" Delayed Replacement Rules, Example 1:", "Subsubsection"],

Cell["\<\
The functional form for a delayed rule   \"lhs \[RuleDelayed] rhs\"  is:  \
RuleDelayed[lhs, rhs].\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.3898396653246555`*^9, 3.3898396695066557`*^9}}],

Cell["\<\
lhs :> rhs represents a rule that transforms lhs to rhs, evaluating rhs only \
when the rule is used.\
\>", "Item",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.3900434768254004`*^9, 3.3900434798044*^9}},
 FontWeight->"Bold"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"  ", 
  RowBox[{"Attributes", " ", "[", "RuleDelayed", "]"}]}]], "Input"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "\nNote that RuleDelayed has attribute ",
 StyleBox["HoldRest",
  FontVariations->{"Underline"->True}],
 " which means that the lhs will be immediately replaced while the rhs will \
be replaced only when the rule is actually used."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.523277574600688*^9}],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"  ", 
  RowBox[{"Clear", " ", "[", 
   RowBox[{"a", ",", "b", ",", "c"}], "]"}]}]], "InputOnly"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"a", "=", "2"}], ";", 
  RowBox[{"b", "=", "3"}], ";", 
  RowBox[{"c", "=", "4"}], ";"}]], "InputOnly"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{" ", 
  RowBox[{"rule2", "=", 
   RowBox[{"b", "\[RuleDelayed]", "c"}]}]}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.3898397359556556`*^9, 3.3898397420206556`*^9}}],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Print", "[", 
  RowBox[{
  "\"\<a = \>\"", ",", "a", ",", "\"\<     b = \>\"", ",", "b", ",", 
   "\"\<     c = \>\"", ",", "c", ",", "\"\<     rule1 = \>\"", ",", 
   "rule2"}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.3898397889356556`*^9, 3.389839789733656*^9}}],

Cell["\<\

Change the value of \"b\" and \"c\":\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.5232775868408103`*^9}],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"b", "=", "5"}], ";", 
  RowBox[{"c", "=", "6"}], ";"}]], "InputOnly"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Print", "[", 
  RowBox[{
  "\"\<a = \>\"", ",", "a", ",", "\"\<     b = \>\"", ",", "b", ",", 
   "\"\<     c = \>\"", ",", "c", ",", "\"\<     rule1 = \>\"", ",", 
   "rule2"}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.3898398063926554`*^9, 3.3898398070396557`*^9}}],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"a", ":=", 
  RowBox[{"b", " ", "/.", "rule2"}]}]], "InputOnly"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"?", "a"}]], "Input"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Print", "[", 
  RowBox[{
  "\"\<a = \>\"", ",", "a", ",", "\"\<     b = \>\"", ",", "b", ",", 
   "\"\<     c = \>\"", ",", "c", ",", "\"\<     rule1 = \>\"", ",", 
   "rule2"}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.3898398425366554`*^9, 3.3898398438976555`*^9}}],

Cell[TextData[{
 "\nThus, the above delayed replacement rule is evaluated as:\n\n\t",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"a", "=", "2"}], ";", 
    RowBox[{"b", "=", "3"}], ";", 
    RowBox[{"c", "=", "4"}], ";"}], TraditionalForm]]],
 "\n\t",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"rule2", "=", 
    RowBox[{"b", "\[RuleDelayed]", "c"}]}], TraditionalForm]]],
 "\n\t",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"rule2", "=", 
    RowBox[{"3", "\[RuleDelayed]", "c"}]}], TraditionalForm]]],
 "\t\t(Note that the lhs has been replaced but the rhs has not)\n\t",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"b", "=", "5"}], ";", 
    RowBox[{"c", "=", "6"}], ";"}], TraditionalForm]]],
 "\t\t(Assign new values for \"b\" and \"c\")\n\t",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"a", ":=", 
    RowBox[{"b", "  ", "/.", "  ", "rule2"}]}], TraditionalForm]]],
 "\n\t",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"a", ":=", 
    RowBox[{"5", "  ", "/.", "  ", "rule2"}]}], TraditionalForm]]],
 "\t(\"b\" is replaced by 5)\n\t",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"a", ":=", 
    RowBox[{"5", "  ", "/.", "  ", 
     RowBox[{"3", "\[RuleDelayed]", "c"}]}]}], TraditionalForm]]],
 "\n\t",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"a", ":=", 
    RowBox[{"5", "  ", "/.", "  ", 
     RowBox[{"3", "\[RuleDelayed]", "6"}]}]}], TraditionalForm]]],
 "\t(\"c\" is replaced by 6)\n\t",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"a", ":=", 
    RowBox[{"5", "  ", "/.", "  ", 
     RowBox[{"3", "\[RuleDelayed]", "6"}]}]}], TraditionalForm]]],
 "\t(Note that the rule is not used)\n\t",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"a", ":=", "5"}], TraditionalForm]]],
 "\n\t5\t\t\t(",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"b", "=", "5"}], ",", 
    RowBox[{"c", "=", "6"}]}], TraditionalForm]]],
 ")"
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.3898398830716553`*^9, 3.3898400098956556`*^9}, 
   3.5232776038809805`*^9}]
}, Closed]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[" Delayed Replacement Rules, Example 2:", "Subsubsection"],

Cell["\<\
As a final example, consider delayed assignment and immediate replacement \
rule on the same line (i.e. evaluated at the same time)\
\>", "Text"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Clear", " ", "[", 
  RowBox[{"a", ",", "b", ",", "c"}], "]"}]], "InputOnly",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.3898401794256554`*^9, 3.389840179681656*^9}}],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"a", "=", "2"}], ";", 
  RowBox[{"b", "=", "3"}], ";", 
  RowBox[{"c", "=", "4"}], ";"}]], "InputOnly"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"a", ":=", 
  RowBox[{"b", " ", "/.", 
   RowBox[{"b", "\[Rule]", "c"}]}]}]], "InputOnly",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.3898401934586554`*^9, 3.389840278695656*^9}],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"?", "a"}]], "Input"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Print", "[", 
  RowBox[{
  "\"\<a = \>\"", ",", "a", ",", "\"\<     b = \>\"", ",", "b", ",", 
   "\"\<     c = \>\"", ",", "c"}], "]"}]], "Input"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "\nThus, the above delayed replacement rule is evaluated as:\n\n\t",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"a", "=", "2"}], ";", 
    RowBox[{"b", "=", "3"}], ";", 
    RowBox[{"c", "=", "4"}], ";"}], TraditionalForm]]],
 "\n\t",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"a", ":=", 
    RowBox[{"b", "  ", "/.", "  ", 
     RowBox[{"b", "\[Rule]", "c"}]}]}], TraditionalForm]]],
 "   \n\t",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"a", ":=", 
    RowBox[{"3", "  ", "/.", "  ", 
     RowBox[{"b", "\[Rule]", "c"}]}]}], TraditionalForm]]],
 "\t(\"b\" is replaced by 5)\n\t",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"a", ":=", 
    RowBox[{"3", "  ", "/.", "  ", 
     RowBox[{"3", "\[Rule]", "4"}]}]}], TraditionalForm]]],
 "\t(\"b\" is replaced by 3 and \"c\" is replaced by 4)\n\t",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"a", ":=", 
    RowBox[{"3", "  ", "/.", "  ", 
     RowBox[{"3", "\[Rule]", "4"}]}]}], TraditionalForm]]],
 "\t(Note that the rule is used)\n\t",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"a", ":=", "4"}], TraditionalForm]]],
 "\n\t4\t\t\t(",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"b", "=", "3"}], ",", 
    RowBox[{"c", "=", "4"}]}], TraditionalForm]]],
 ")"
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.3898403126666555`*^9, 3.3898404396856556`*^9}, 
   3.5232777088920307`*^9}],

Cell["\<\
Thus, the use of delayed assignment and immediate replacement rule on the \
same line will not generate assignment conflicts.
\
\>", "Text"]
}, Closed]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[" Clearing Before Replacement Rules and Assignments:", "Subsubsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.5232777339722815`*^9}],

Cell["\<\
It is important to realize that if no values have been assigned to:  a, b and \
c, then all of the above examples will yield the same result.

Immediate replacement rule:\
\>", "Text"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Clear", " ", "[", 
  RowBox[{"a", ",", "b", ",", "c"}], "]"}]], "InputOnly",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.3898404868516555`*^9, 3.3898404870606556`*^9}}],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"rule1", "=", 
  RowBox[{"b", "\[Rule]", "c"}]}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.389840499082656*^9, 3.389840511209656*^9}}],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"a", ":=", 
  RowBox[{"b", " ", "/.", "rule1"}]}]], "InputOnly",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.3898405145476556`*^9, 3.389840515766656*^9}}],

Cell[BoxData["a"], "Input"],

Cell["\<\

Delayed replacement rule:\
\>", "Text"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"  ", 
  RowBox[{"Clear", " ", "[", 
   RowBox[{"a", ",", "b", ",", "c"}], "]"}]}]], "InputOnly"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{" ", 
  RowBox[{"rule2", "=", 
   RowBox[{"b", "\[RuleDelayed]", "c"}]}]}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.389840539636656*^9, 3.389840540667656*^9}}],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"a", ":=", 
  RowBox[{"b", " ", "/.", "rule2"}]}]], "InputOnly"],

Cell[BoxData["a"], "Input"],

Cell["\<\

Immediate replacement rule on same line as delayed assignment:\
\>", "Text"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"  ", 
  RowBox[{"Clear", " ", "[", 
   RowBox[{"a", ",", "b", ",", "c"}], "]"}]}]], "InputOnly"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"a", ":=", 
  RowBox[{"b", " ", "/.", 
   RowBox[{"b", "\[Rule]", "c"}]}]}]], "InputOnly",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.3898405606756554`*^9, 3.3898405619636555`*^9}}],

Cell[BoxData["a"], "Input"],

Cell["\<\

Observe that in each of the above examples, the value of \"a\" remains the \
same.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.523277754232484*^9}]
}, Closed]]
}, Closed]]
}, Closed]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox[" Exercises", "Title"],
 "  Advanced Lesson 11 "
}], "Section"],

Cell["\<\
Your Name:

Your Math Class:\
\>", "Program",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.390368232619*^9, 3.3903682391219997`*^9}, {
   3.390368866851*^9, 3.390368908736*^9}, {3.3903690435030003`*^9, 
   3.390369082222*^9}, 3.3903880065649595`*^9},
 FontSize->16,
 FontWeight->"Bold"]
}, Closed]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[" Pattern matching in functional arguments:", "Section"],

Cell["\<\
When you are instructed to construct a function whose argument will match \
exactly one arbitrary object, you will write:   f[ x_ ]
 If you want delayed assignment to that function you will write:   f[ x_ ]  \
:=  rhs[ x ]\
\>", "Text"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "1: Write a delayed assignment function of exactly one argument which will \
square the argument.\n\tEvaluate:   ? f\n\tEvaluate:   f[2]\n\tEvaluate:   \
f[x]\n\tEvaluate:   f[y]\t\t",
 StyleBox["\[DoubleLongRightArrow] ",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   SuperscriptBox["y", "2"],
   FontWeight->"Bold"]]],
 "\n\tEvaluate:   f[\"string\"]\n\tEvaluate:   f[ {1,2,3} ]\n\tEvaluate:   f[ \
",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"(", "\[NegativeThinSpace]", GridBox[{
      {"1", "2"},
      {"3", "4"}
     }], "\[NegativeThinSpace]", ")"}], TraditionalForm]]],
 " ]\t\t",
 StyleBox["\[DoubleLongRightArrow] ",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 "{{1,4},{9,16}}",
 "\n\tEvaluate:   f[ ]\n\tEvaluate:   f[ x,y ]\n\tEvaluate:   f[ 1,2,3,4 ]\n \
Explain what is different about the last three evaluations."
}], "Text"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "2: Write a delayed assignment function of EXACTLY ZERO arguments which will \
take on the value 3.\n\tEvaluate:   ? f\n\tEvaluate:   f[ ]\t\t\t",
 StyleBox["\[DoubleLongRightArrow] 3",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 "\n\tEvaluate:   f[2]\n\tEvaluate:   f[x]\n\tEvaluate:   f[ x,y ]\n\t\
Evaluate:   f[ 1,2,3,4 ]\n\tEvaluate:   f[ ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"(", "\[NegativeThinSpace]", GridBox[{
      {"1", "2"},
      {"3", "4"}
     }], "\[NegativeThinSpace]", ")"}], TraditionalForm]]],
 " ]\n Explain what is different about the last five evaluations."
}], "Text"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "3: Write a delayed assignment function of ONE OR MORE arguments which will \
square the LIST of arguments.\n\tDoes the square (i.e. Power) have attribute \
Listable?  What does this mean?\n\tEvaluate:   ? f\n\tEvaluate:   f[2]\n\t\
Evaluate:   f[x]\n\tEvaluate:   f[y]\t\t\t",
 StyleBox["\[DoubleLongRightArrow]  ",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"{", 
   SuperscriptBox["y", "2"], "}"}]],
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 StyleBox["  ",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 "\n\tEvaluate:   f[\"string\"]\n\tEvaluate:   f[ {1,2,3} ]\t\t\t",
 StyleBox["\[DoubleLongRightArrow] ",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 "{{1,4,9}}\n\tEvaluate:   f[ ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"(", "\[NegativeThinSpace]", GridBox[{
      {"1", "2"},
      {"3", "4"}
     }], "\[NegativeThinSpace]", ")"}], TraditionalForm]]],
 " ]\n\tEvaluate:   f[ x,y ]\n\tEvaluate:   f[ 1,2,3,4 ]\n\tEvaluate:   f[ x, \
{1,2,3} ]\t\t",
 StyleBox["\[DoubleLongRightArrow] ",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"{", 
   RowBox[{
    SuperscriptBox["x", "2"], ",", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"1", ",", "4", ",", "9"}], "}"}]}], "}"}]],
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 "\n\tEvaluate:   f[ x, {1,2,3}, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"(", "\[NegativeThinSpace]", GridBox[{
      {"1", "2"},
      {"3", "4"}
     }], "\[NegativeThinSpace]", ")"}], TraditionalForm]]],
 " ]\n\tEvaluate:   f[ ]\n Explain what is different about the last \
evaluation."
}], "Text"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "4: Write a delayed assignment function of ZERO OR MORE arguments which will \
square the LIST of arguments.\n\tEvaluate:   ? f\n\tEvaluate:   f[2]\n\t\
Evaluate:   f[x]\n\tEvaluate:   f[y]\n\tEvaluate:   f[\"string\"]\n\t\
Evaluate:   f[ {1,2,3} ]\t\t\t",
 StyleBox["\[DoubleLongRightArrow] ",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 "{{1,4,9}}\n\tEvaluate:   f[ ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"(", "\[NegativeThinSpace]", GridBox[{
      {"1", "2"},
      {"3", "4"}
     }], "\[NegativeThinSpace]", ")"}], TraditionalForm]]],
 " ]\n\tEvaluate:   f[ x,y ]\n\tEvaluate:   f[ 1,2,3,4 ]\n\tEvaluate:   f[ x, \
{1,2,3} ]\t\t",
 StyleBox["\[DoubleLongRightArrow] ",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"{", 
   RowBox[{
    SuperscriptBox["x", "2"], ",", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"1", ",", "4", ",", "9"}], "}"}]}], "}"}]],
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 "\n\tEvaluate:   f[ x, {1,2,3}, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"(", "\[NegativeThinSpace]", GridBox[{
      {"1", "2"},
      {"3", "4"}
     }], "\[NegativeThinSpace]", ")"}], TraditionalForm]]],
 " ]\n\tEvaluate:   f[ ]\n Explain the last evaluation."
}], "Text"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "5: Write a delayed assignment function of exactly TWO arguments which will \
square the first argument times the Sine of the second argument.\n\tEvaluate: \
  ? f\n\tEvaluate:   f[ ]\n\tEvaluate:   f[x]\n\tEvaluate:   f[ {1,2} ]\n\t\
Evaluate:   f[ {1,2,3} ]\n\tEvaluate:   f[ 1,2,3,4 ]\n\tEvaluate:   f[ x,y ]\t\
\t\t",
 StyleBox["\[DoubleLongRightArrow]  ",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox["x", "2"], " ", 
   RowBox[{"Sin", "[", "y", "]"}]}]],
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 "\n\tEvaluate:   f[ x, {1,2,3} ]\n\tEvaluate:   f[ \"string\", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"(", "\[NegativeThinSpace]", GridBox[{
      {"1", "2"},
      {"3", "4"}
     }], "\[NegativeThinSpace]", ")"}], TraditionalForm]]],
 " ]\n Explain why the first five evaluations did not work."
}], "Text"],

Cell["\<\
6: Part 1: Write a delayed assignment function of exactly THREE arguments \
which equals the list of those three arguments.
 Part 2: Write a delayed assignment function of exactly FOUR arguments which \
equals the list of those four arguments.\
\>", "Text"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "7: Write a delayed assignment function of exactly ONE argument followed by \
ZERO or more arguments which will square the first argument times the Sine of \
the LIST of the second arguments.\n\tEvaluate:   ? f\n\tEvaluate:   f[ ]\n\t\
Evaluate:   f[x]\t  \[DoubleLongRightArrow]  { },  How did ",
 StyleBox["Mathematica",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " calculate this value?\n\tEvaluate:   f[ {1,2} ]\t  Why did ",
 StyleBox["Mathematica ",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 "fail to calculate this value?\n\tEvaluate:   f[ x,y ]\t\t  \
\[DoubleLongRightArrow] ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     SuperscriptBox["x", "2"], " ", 
     RowBox[{"Sin", "[", "y", "]"}]}], "}"}],
   FontWeight->"Bold"]]],
 "\n\tEvaluate:   f[ 2,3,4,5 ]\t  \[DoubleLongRightArrow]  {4 Sin[3],4 \
Sin[4],4 Sin[5]}\n\tEvaluate:   f[ x, y, z, w ]\n\tEvaluate:   f[ x, {1,2,3}, \
A, B ]\tLook at this result in:  ColumnForm,  \n\t\t\t\t\t\tHow did ",
 StyleBox["Mathematica",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " calculate this value?\n\tEvaluate:   f[ \"string\", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"(", "\[NegativeThinSpace]", GridBox[{
      {"1", "2"},
      {"3", "4"}
     }], "\[NegativeThinSpace]", ")"}], TraditionalForm]]],
 " ]"
}], "Text"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "8: Write a delayed assignment function of the Sine of exactly one argument \
which will square the argument which appears inside the Sine function.\n\t\
Evaluate:   ? f\n\tEvaluate:   f[ Sin[2] ]\t\t  \[DoubleLongRightArrow] 4\n\t\
Evaluate:   f[ Sin[y] ]\n\tEvaluate:   f[ Sin[ {1,2,3} ] ]\t  Why did ",
 StyleBox["Mathematica ",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 "fail to match this pattern?\n\tEvaluate:   f[ Sin[ Log[x] ] ]\n\tEvaluate:  \
 f[x]\n\tEvaluate:   f[ Cos[y] ]\n\tEvaluate:   f[ 1,2,3,4 ]\n Explain what \
is different about the last three evaluations."
}], "Text"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "9: Write a delayed assignment function which will have several different \
assignments.  Specifically,  f[ function[ x_ ] ] :=  derivative[ x ] for \
different functions (\"f\" will be defined using multiple assignments.  Also, \
\"f\" will ",
 StyleBox["NOT",
  FontVariations->{"Underline"->True}],
 " use the chain rule correctly, i.e. f[ Sin[2x] ]\t\[DoubleLongRightArrow] \
Cos[ 2x ]   ",
 StyleBox["NOT",
  FontVariations->{"Underline"->True}],
 "  2 Cos[ 2x ]).  \"f\" should use pattern matching to accept as arguments \
the functions:   Sin[x], Cos[x], Log[x], ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox["E", "x"], TraditionalForm]]],
 "   and return the corresponding  \"derivative\" functions.\n\tEvaluate:   ? \
f\n\tEvaluate:   f[ ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox["\[ExponentialE]", "x"], TraditionalForm]]],
 " ]\n\tEvaluate:   f[ Sin[y] ]\t\t\[DoubleLongRightArrow] Cos[ y ]\n\t\
Evaluate:   f[ Cos[x + y] ]\n\tEvaluate:   f[ Sin[2] ]\t\t\
\[DoubleLongRightArrow] Cos[ 2 ]\n\tEvaluate:   f[ Sin[ Log[x] ] ]\n\t\
Evaluate:   f[ Sin[ {1,2,3} ] ]\t  Why did ",
 StyleBox["Mathematica ",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 "fail to match this pattern?"
}], "Text"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "10:  Odd functions have the property that:  f( -x )  \
\[DoubleLongRightArrow]  -f( x ).  Write a delayed assignment function which \
uses pattern matching which will make this assignment.  (Note that this is a \
recursive assignment.)\n\tEvaluate:   ? f\n\tEvaluate:   f[ -x ]\n\tEvaluate: \
  f[ -y ]\t\t\[DoubleLongRightArrow] - f[ y ]\n\tEvaluate:   f[ -Sin[y] ]\n\t\
Evaluate:   f[ -5 ]\tWhy did ",
 StyleBox["Mathematica ",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 "fail to match this pattern?  \n\t\t\t\tHint: look at FullForm[ -5 ]  and  \
FullForm[ -x ]"
}], "Text"],

Cell["\<\
11:  How would you add a new assignment to the function \"f\" in Problem 10 \
so that the function \"f\" with two assignments would also accept the \
pattern:   f( -5 )  \[DoubleLongRightArrow]  -f( 5 ) for different negative \
numbers?  (There are several correct ways to do this.)
\tEvaluate:   ? f
\tEvaluate:   f[ -x ]\t\t\[DoubleLongRightArrow] - f[ x ]
\tEvaluate:   f[ x ]
\tEvaluate:   f[ -y ]
\tEvaluate:   f[ -Sin[y] ]
\tEvaluate:   f[ -5 ]\t\t\[DoubleLongRightArrow] - f[ 5 ]
\tEvaluate:   f[ -7 ]
\tEvaluate:   f[ 5 ]\
\>", "Text"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "12: Write a delayed assignment function using pattern matching that will \
accept as its argument a list (of 3 or more elements) which will return the \
value of the third element in the list.  \n\tEvaluate:   ? f\n\tEvaluate:   \
f[ ]\t\tWhy did ",
 StyleBox["Mathematica ",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 "fail to match this pattern?\n\tEvaluate:   f[x]\tWhy did ",
 StyleBox["Mathematica ",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 "fail to match this pattern?\n\tEvaluate:   f[ {1,2} ]\tWhy did ",
 StyleBox["Mathematica ",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 "fail to match this pattern?\n\tEvaluate:   f[ {1,2,3} ] \t\
\[DoubleLongRightArrow] 3\n\tEvaluate:   f[ {1,2,3,4} ]\n\tEvaluate:   f[ \
{1,2,3,4,5} ]\n\tEvaluate:   f[ {x,y, {1,2,3}, A, B }]\t"
}], "Text"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "13: Write a delayed assignment function using pattern matching that will \
accept as its argument:\n\tA list of elements,\n\tWhich contains another list \
(of 1 or more elements)\t\n\tWhich will return the inside list of elements.  \
\n\tEvaluate:   ? f\n\tEvaluate:   f[ 1, 2, {4, 5}, 6 ]\t\tWhy did ",
 StyleBox["Mathematica ",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 "fail to match this pattern?\n\tEvaluate:   f[ {1, 2, 3, 4} ]\t\tWhy did ",
 StyleBox["Mathematica ",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 "fail to match this pattern?\n\tEvaluate:   f[ {1, 2, { }, 3, 4} ]\tWhy did ",
 StyleBox["Mathematica ",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 "fail to match this pattern?\n\tEvaluate:   f[ {{1}, 2, 3, 4} ] \t\t\
\[DoubleLongRightArrow] {1}\n\tEvaluate:   f[ {1, 2, {3}, 4} ] \t\t\
\[DoubleLongRightArrow] {3}\n\tEvaluate:   f[ {1, {2, 3}, 4} ] \t\t\
\[DoubleLongRightArrow] {2, 3}\n\tEvaluate:   f[ {1, 2, 3, {4}} ] \t\t\
\[DoubleLongRightArrow] {4}\n\tEvaluate:   f[ {1, 2, {3, 4, 5}} ]\n\t\
Evaluate:   f[ {{1, 2, 3, 4, 5}} ]\n\tEvaluate:   f[ {1, 2, {3,{ 4, 5}}} ]\n\t\
Evaluate:   f[ {x, y, {1,2,3}, A, B }]\t"
}], "Text"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "14: Calculate the FullForm[...] of each expression ",
 StyleBox["inside",
  FontVariations->{"Underline"->True}],
 " the quotation marks:\n\t\"_\"           \[DoubleLongRightArrow]  ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"Blank", "[", "]"}], TraditionalForm]]],
 "\n\t\"x_\"\n\t\"x__\"\n\t\"x___\"\t\n\t\"x_Integer\"\n\t\"x_?EvenQ\"\n\t\
\"x_?(# > 3&)\"\n\t\"x_Integer?EvenQ\"\nCreate a function which will return \
the character string \"Positive Integer\" when its argument is a positive \
integer and have the function remain unevaluated under all other \
circumstances.  Your function should use pattern matching similar to the last \
entry given above:\n  \t",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"f", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"x_.", ".."}], "?"}], "..."}], "]"}], ":=", " "}], 
   TraditionalForm]]],
 "\"Positive Integer\"\nEvaluate:\n\t",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"f", "[", "3", "]"}], TraditionalForm]]],
 "\n\t",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"f", "[", "3.45", "]"}], TraditionalForm]]],
 "\n\t",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"f", "[", 
     RowBox[{"-", "3"}], "]"}], " "}], TraditionalForm]]]
}], "Text"]
}, Closed]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[" Pattern matching in replacement rules:", "Section"],

Cell["\<\
When you are instructed to construct an immediate replacement rule you will \
write:   lhs \[Rule] rhs
When you are instructed to construct a delayed replacement rule you will \
write:   lhs \[RuleDelayed] rhs
When you are instructed to apply the replacement rule to an expression you \
will write: 
\t  expression(   ...   lhs  ...  )      /.     lhs \[Rule] rhs 
which will yield:
\t  expression(   ...  rhs  ...  )\
\>", "Text"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "14: Write an immediate replacement rule which pattern matches 2 and \
replaces it with 222 and assign this rule to: rule1.  Apply this replacement \
rule to the following expressions:\n\tEvaluate:   ? rule1\t\t\t\
\[DoubleLongRightArrow]   rule1 =  2 \[Rule] 222\n\tEvaluate:   {1, 2, 3, 4}  \
/.  rule1\t\[DoubleLongRightArrow]   {1,222,3,4}\n\tEvaluate:   Sin[ 2 ]  /.  \
rule1\n\tEvaluate:   {1, 2, Sin[ 2 ], ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox["x", 
    RowBox[{"2", " "}]], TraditionalForm]]],
 "}  /.  rule1\t\n\tEvaluate:   {1, 2, 3, 2+2}  /.  rule1\t Why was the last \
replacement missed?\n\tEvaluate:   {1, 2, 3, Hold[ 2+2 ]}  /.  rule1\n\t\
Evaluate:    2 Sin[ 2 Sin[ 2 Sin[ 2 Sin[ 2 x] ] ] ]  /.  rule1"
}], "Text"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "15: Write an immediate replacement rule which pattern matches ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox[
    RowBox[{"(", "x_", ")"}], "3"], TraditionalForm]]],
 " and replaces it with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox["x", "333"], TraditionalForm]]],
 " and assign this rule to: rule2.  Apply this replacement rule to the \
following expressions:\n\tEvaluate:   ? rule2\t\t\t\[DoubleLongRightArrow]   \
rule2 =  ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox[
    RowBox[{"(", "x_", ")"}], "3"], TraditionalForm]]],
 " \[Rule] ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox["x", "333"], TraditionalForm]]],
 "\n\tEvaluate:   ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{" ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"{", " ", 
     RowBox[{
      SuperscriptBox["x", "2"], ",", " ", 
      SuperscriptBox["x", "3"], ",", " ", 
      SuperscriptBox["x", "4"], ",", " ", 
      SuperscriptBox["y", "3"], ",", " ", 
      SuperscriptBox[
       RowBox[{"Sin", "[", "x", "]"}], "3"], ",", " ", 
      FractionBox["1", 
       RowBox[{"2", "+", 
        SuperscriptBox["z", "3"]}]], " ", ",", " ", 
      SuperscriptBox[
       RowBox[{"(", 
        RowBox[{"x", "+", "y"}], ")"}], "3"]}], "}"}], "/.", "  ", 
    "rule2"}]}]],
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 "\n\tEvaluate:   ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"(", 
      FractionBox["1", 
       RowBox[{"2", "+", "y"}]], ")"}], "3"], "/.", "  ", "rule2"}],
   FontWeight->"Bold"]]],
 "\t Why was the last replacement missed?\n\tLook at the following to answer \
the above question:\n\tEvaluate:    ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"FullForm", "[", 
   SuperscriptBox["x", "3"], "]"}]],
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 "\n\tEvaluate:    ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"FullForm", "[", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{"2", "+", "y"}], ")"}], "3"], "]"}]],
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 "\n\tEvaluate:    ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Hold", "[", 
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"(", 
      FractionBox["1", 
       RowBox[{"2", "+", "y"}]], ")"}], "3"], "]"}], "/.", "  ", "rule2"}]],
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 "\n\tEvaluate:    ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"FullForm", "[", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    RowBox[{"(", 
     FractionBox["1", 
      RowBox[{"2", "+", "y"}]], ")"}], "3"], "]"}]],
  FontWeight->"Bold"]
}], "Text"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "16: Make a list of the previous two rules.  Apply this list of replacement \
rules to the following expressions: \n\tEvaluate:   ? {rule1, rule2}\t\n\t\
Evaluate:   ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{" ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"{", " ", 
     RowBox[{
      SuperscriptBox["x", "2"], ",", " ", 
      SuperscriptBox["x", "3"], ",", " ", 
      SuperscriptBox["x", "4"], ",", " ", 
      SuperscriptBox["y", "3"], ",", " ", 
      SuperscriptBox[
       RowBox[{"Sin", "[", "x", "]"}], "3"], ",", " ", 
      FractionBox["1", 
       RowBox[{"2", "+", 
        SuperscriptBox["z", "3"]}]], " ", ",", " ", 
      SuperscriptBox[
       RowBox[{"(", 
        RowBox[{"x", "+", "y"}], ")"}], "3"]}], "}"}], "/.", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"rule1", ",", " ", "rule2"}], "}"}]}]}]],
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 "\n\tEvaluate:   ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{
       StyleBox["2",
        FontWeight->"Bold"], "+", "y"}], ")"}], "3"], "/.", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"rule1", ",", " ", "rule2"}], "}"}]}],
   FontWeight->"Bold"]]],
 "\tWhy was the first replacement missed?\n\tEvaluate:   ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{
       StyleBox["2",
        FontWeight->"Bold"], "+", "y"}], ")"}], "3"], "//.", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"rule1", ",", " ", "rule2"}], "}"}]}],
   FontWeight->"Bold"]]],
 "\tWhy did this work?"
}], "Text"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "17: The following example illustrates some of the power of pattern matching \
and replacement rules.  As you already know, every operation in ",
 StyleBox["Mathematica",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " has an internal functional representation.  \n\nFor example, generate the \
plot of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   SuperscriptBox["x", "2"],
   FontWeight->"Bold"]]],
 " and assign the output to:  plot1.\n\n\tEvaluate:   ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"plot1", "=", 
   RowBox[{"Plot", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     SuperscriptBox["x", "2"], ",", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"x", ",", "0", ",", "1"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}]],
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 "\n\n  To display the internal functional representation:\n  \n\tEvaluate:   \
? plot1\n\n Observe that the contents of plot1 is something like:  \n \n   \
plot1 = ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"Graphics", "[", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", " ", "}"}], ",", 
       RowBox[{"{", " ", "}"}], ",", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"Hue", "[", 
          RowBox[{"0.67`", ",", "0.6`", ",", "0.6`"}], "]"}], ",", 
         RowBox[{"Line", "[", 
          RowBox[{"{", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"{", 
             RowBox[{
             "2.040816326530612`*^-8", ",", "4.1649312786339017`*^-16"}], 
             "}"}], ","}]}]}]}]}]}]}]}]}], TraditionalForm]]],
 " .........\n \nalong with a list of replacement rules for graphic options.  \
The first part consists of the Line command, which just connects a sequence \
of line segments through a list of coordinates  {{x1,y1}, {x2,y2},  ...  }.  \
\n\n Our objective is to replace the line segments with a list of points \
using pattern matching and replacement rules.  To accomplish this, we need to \
understand the pattern in the Line command as well as the Point command.  The \
patterns are as follows:\n \n \tThe pattern we have:   Line [{{x1,y1}, \
{x2,y2},  ...  }]\n \tThe pattern we want:  {Point [{x1,y1}], Point \
[{x2,y2}],  ...  }\n \t \n Thus, we want to use pattern matching and \
replacement rules to replace:\n \n \t Line [{  ...  , {x,y},  ...  }]\n \t \n \
with:\n \n  \t {  ...  , Point [{x,y}],  ...  }\n  \t \n This can be \
accomplished in two steps.  Replace the content in plot1 by creating a \
replacement rule from:   \n \t\n \tLine [{  ...  , {x,y},  ...  }]  \[Rule]  \
Line [{  ...  , Point [{x,y}],  ...  }]\n \t\t\n to get an intermediate step \
(call it plot2).  plot2 will NOT be a proper plot, so it can not be \
displayed.  The graphic display can be suppressed by ending with a \";\".  \
Then to see the content of plot2:\n \n \tEvaluate:   ? plot2\n \t\nThen \
replace the content in plot2 by creating a replacement rule from:   \n \t\n \t\
Line [{  ...  , Point [{x,y}],  ...  }] \[Rule]  {  ...  , Point [{x,y}],  \
...  }\n \t\t\n to get our final graphic commands (call it plot3).  Then to \
see the content of plot3:\n \n \tEvaluate:   ? plot3\n \t\n plot3 will be a \
proper plot, so it can be displayed.\n \n\tEvaluate:   plot3 \n\t\nYou should \
conclude that EVERY ",
 StyleBox["Mathematica",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " expression, no matter what its form, can be manipulated in this way."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.39047221126*^9, 3.390472267766*^9}, 3.390473108457*^9, {
   3.390473186025*^9, 3.3904734621689997`*^9}}],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Print",
  FontSize->14,
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 StyleBox[" your homework exercises",
  FontSize->14],
 ".\n",
 StyleBox["But do ",
  FontSize->14,
  FontWeight->"Bold",
  FontColor->RGBColor[1, 0, 0]],
 StyleBox["NOT",
  FontSize->18,
  FontWeight->"Bold",
  FontColor->RGBColor[1, 0, 0]],
 StyleBox[" print the above lesson along with the exercises!",
  FontSize->14,
  FontWeight->"Bold",
  FontColor->RGBColor[1, 0, 0]]
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.3903491193324003`*^9, 3.3903491706104*^9}, {
   3.3903492171244*^9, 3.3903492363613997`*^9}, {3.3903493057854*^9, 
